  "body": "## What changed\n`docs_images_match_the_rendered_steps` (from #525, by @tbrasselle) compared pixel goldens in the default ui suite and fails on Linux adapters. Split in two:\n- `docs_example_steps_through_operations` (default suite, every OS): the example opens, every operation has a toolpath, each step draws an overlay.\n- `docs_images_snapshot_match_the_rendered_steps`: the PNG compare, `#[ignore]`d with its lane named (#255).\n- `xtask/src/plan.rs`: the release plan gets a `--test gpu_render --ignored snapshot` step, since the existing snapshot step is `--lib` only and would never reach this integration binary. xtask unit test updated. Process file change: `PROCESS_VERSION` 12 -> 13 (a fork must re-sync xtask).\n- PNGs untouched. Decision: `docs/decisions/854-docs-images-lane.md`.\n\n## Tested\n- `cargo test -p xtask` 30 pass; `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run` lists the new step [14].\n- `docs_example_steps_through_operations` passes locally (macOS); the ignored snapshot still reports drift on this Mac's adapter too, so it is adapter-dependent and belongs in the release lane.\n- Linux gate: run after push (see PR comment).\n\nNot exercised: a full release tier.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nFork synced at v0.17.0\n\n**Gates:**\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 30 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run`: lists `[14] ui gpu_render snapshot lane (debug --ignored)`.\n- Linux quick gate (base upstream/main): green.\n- `docs_example_steps_through_operations --exact`: green on Linux and macOS.\n\n**Note for the cut:** the ignored pixel compare ALSO drifts on macOS (about 5,500 px per image), so the committed PNGs are stale against the current renderer, not just off-platform. The release tier will flag them, and the goldens get regenerated at the cut after a human look (the #255 snapshot rule). This PR leaves the PNGs untouched.\n\nFixes #854\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
